Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8edd9aae-aaf7-1a40-b86b-dc681d163711"],

Cell["\<\
Real NMR probes experience continuous distributions of chemical-shift \
offsets, spatial RF field (B1) inhomogeneity, and scalar/dipolar coupling \
spread. Robust ensemble GRAPE replaces a single system Hamiltonian with a \
weighted sample grid over uncertainty parameters, optimising one shared \
waveform across all members simultaneously.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1180feed-b8d1-1a4d-99c1-d3d228a04f82"],

Cell["\<\
Build 1D and 2D OptimalControlEnsemble grids using EnsembleParameters and \
RFInhomogeneity.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f535547c-e58f-5e48-a081-33b59b780931"],

Cell["\<\
Understand the Fourier resolution criterion (delta_nu <= 1/(2T)) that \
prevents destructive inter-grid aliasing nulls.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"730ec2c1-c65d-bd4e-adc5-7ba3db2fa340"],

Cell["\<\
Contrast EnsembleAggregation -> \"Mean\" against {\"SoftMin\", beta} driven \
with SoftMinSchedule and TimeStepSchedule.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5032a56d-78e5-9b4e-8b7b-fa4266d6fc36"],

Cell["\<\
Verify generalisation on an independent dense grid using \
EvaluateEnsembleFidelity and inspect individual off-resonance trajectories \
interactively.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"11959b14-1c39-a84f-a293-91eb4d7ade5d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Mathematical Background", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1915a638-1b01-d941-a420-dc38b07a778c"],

Cell["\<\
Given normalised member weights w_alpha > 0 (Sum w_alpha = 1), \"Mean\" \
maximises Phi_Mean = Sum w_alpha s_alpha (where s_alpha = Phi_alpha + \
Phi_run,alpha), whereas {\"SoftMin\", beta} maximises the smooth log-sum-exp \
lower bound min s_alpha - beta^-1 Log[Sum w_alpha Exp[-beta (s_alpha - min \
s)]]. Its exact gradient automatically reweights every member by its softmax \
Boltzmann factor w_alpha^eff ~ w_alpha Exp[-beta s_alpha], focusing optimiser \
effort onto the weakest parameter corner.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b7660e3-d0c2-5545-b2cc-5d43adf13575"],

Cell["\<\
Because a pulse of duration T = 2 ms has Fourier frequency resolution ~ 1/T = \
0.5 kHz, training offsets spaced at >= 1.0 kHz leave inter-grid gaps wide \
enough for narrowband destructive interference between sample points. Always \
choose grid spacing <= 1/(2T) and verify on a 2x\[Dash]4x finer test grid.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fe9a21cf-74bc-2c45-aed9-b66df5345f11"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Worked Example", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7984900c-3f7d-3444-ab19-62972189c5a7"],

Cell["\<\
Compare undersampled 11-point training (step 1.0 kHz) against properly \
sampled 21-point (step 0.5 kHz) and 41-point (step 0.25 kHz) broadband [-5, \
+5] kHz inversion pulses evaluated on a 101-point dense grid, followed by a \
2D Offset x RF inhomogeneity continuation design.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0e90f10e-1008-754e-8acd-45c9c46b7bdb"],

