     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"rfScale", ",", " ", "1.0", ",", " ", "\"\<B1 Scale\>\""}], 
      "}"}], ",", " ", "0.8", ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "0.05", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Appearance", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Labeled\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "\n", "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"297e096c-c6df-8849-9a03-\
e0e0bcd162d7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Suggested Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6acb2fe0-f3e9-7946-870a-0086f78e905e"],

Cell["\<\
1. Observe Nyquist grid aliasing: Set Training Step = 1.0 kHz at \
Half-Bandwidth = 4.0 kHz in Lab 5A. Training Min looks > 0.99, while \
Out-of-Sample Min craters between the red training markers! Switch Step to \
0.25 kHz to cure it completely.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d7dbcfdf-1f68-4d43-a491-3d810fdec41f"],

Cell["\<\
2. Mean vs SoftMin corners: Switch Aggregation from \"Mean\" to \"SoftMin(30)\
\" with SoftMinSchedule enabled and observe how edge fidelities rise \
uniformly.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2e1376aa-7f40-714e-b266-0d80521a3870"],

Cell["\<\
3. 2D Stress Test: Enable +/-15% RF Inhomogeneity in Lab 5A, then scrub both \
extremes in Lab 5B to see how compensation twists the trajectories near t = \
T/2 so every spin refocuses at t = T.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d42dd60d-ab57-a54d-8d65-9827c8709fe8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5aed77c9-9d7e-4d4d-b66d-9920f663aa87"],

Cell["\<\
Ensemble GRAPE designs broadband, B1-tolerant pulses that remain smooth out \
of sample provided the training grid honours the Fourier spacing bound <= \
1/(2T) and uses SoftMin continuation to raise worst-case members uniformly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a34487c0-b915-0349-86ca-76c7b1657132"],

